  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the implementation of PEAS programme through development of a climate sensitive curriculum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is implementing innovative approaches to strengthening the education system to expand provision of secondary education, and to improve quality education outcomes for the most disadvantaged children in Zambia. As part of the programme, PEAS aims to scale its network of rural secondary schools to increase access to the most marginalised students (at least 50% girls) and to reach school-level sustainability. PEAS will also strengthen the equity and quality of education in the PEAS network, develop school improvement tools and generate evidence on what works to improve inclusion, teaching quality and outcomes for girls to share with the Government.

PEAS delivers this objective through a collaborative approach with Government of Zambia in demonstrating how to improve the inclusivity, quality, and efficiency of secondary education. PEAS operates secondary schools in partnership with the GRZ in Copperbelt, Northern, Southern and Muchinga Province.</narrative>
  </description>
